    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>One-week review after CT coronary angiography and upper endoscopy this morning. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Aurelius returns one week after his first visit. He had CT coronary angiography early this morning and an upper endoscopy afterwards with Dr. Brandt-Oyelaran of gastroenterology, and has recovered from the sedation. Over the week the burning in his upper abdomen and lower chest has continued after his late evening meal, waking him twice with a sour taste; calcium carbonate eases it within minutes. He has had no pain on exertion, no breathlessness and no fainting. He collected the naloxone spray and keeps it by his bed. He took his herbal paste on most nights as before and drank no wine on those nights. He has used polyethylene glycol twice, with softer stools. The first CBT-I session could not be booked this week. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Burning after the evening meal, night waking twice; eased by antacid; no exertional pain</td></tr><tr><td>Testing today</td><td>CT coronary angiography; upper endoscopy with gastric biopsies and a rapid urease test</td></tr><tr><td>Remedy</td><td>Most nights as before; no wine on those nights; naloxone at home</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Negative</td><td>No exertional chest pain, palpitations or fainting</td></tr><tr><td>Gastrointestinal</td><td>Positive</td><td>Burning after the evening meal with a sour taste; no difficulty swallowing, vomiting or black stools; stools softer</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Negative</td><td>No breathlessness or cough</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Positive</td><td>Poor sleep; mood steady; no thoughts of self-harm</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>4 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

